Package: scStable
Type: Package
Title: Generation of Synthetic Single-Cell RNA-seq Replicates from Bulk RNA-seq
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "First",
           family = "Last",
           email = "you@example.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: scStable generates synthetic single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq)
    replicates by combining a fitted bulk RNA-seq distribution with a
    single-cell generative model (scDesign3). Given a reference bulk RNA-seq
    matrix and a reference scRNA-seq matrix, scStable fits a multivariate model
    to the bulk data, samples new synthetic bulk profiles, and propagates the
    induced per-gene variation into newly simulated single-cell count matrices,
    yielding biologically plausible synthetic replicates for benchmarking and
    method-stability evaluation. When no paired bulk RNA-seq sample is available
    for the single-cell data, scStable can instead use a publicly available bulk
    reference from the same tissue (e.g. GTEx) as a surrogate anchor via
    synthreplicate_from_tissue().
